@import "Exercise_8_21.lean"

**EXERCISE 8.21.** Using the fixed-point construction, show that there is a continuous and computable operator $\lambda a.\, a^{\S}$, such that if $a$ is a finitary projection of $U$, then

$$D_{a^{\S}} \cong (D_a)^{\S} \ .$$

The development is with the [A-sharp on lists](1980_ASharp.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`example_821`).** The list-of-projection combinator is finitary when the projection is finitary.

*Proof.* By assembling the peer lemmas named in the packaging module. ∎
